}", "language": "json", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "This complete example demonstrates a production-grade workspace template. It explicitly references the dotnet process runner, specifies relative path arguments, and injects controlled environment variables. Inspecting templates like this ensures workspace settings adhere strictly to validation requirements before public test execution.", "los": ["CO1.LO1"], "sources": [], "minutes": 9}, {"kind": "worked_problem", "title": "Spotting Schema and Protocol Violations", "bullets": ["Problem: Analyze a flawed workspace config, identify schema bugs, and correct them.", "Flaw 1: Missing command key in stdio transport definition.", "Flaw 2: Invalid primitive type in env map (e.g., numeric integer instead of string).", "Solution: Add required command path and cast all env map values to string scalars."], "figure": {"kind": "code", "caption": "Buggy Configuration vs Fixed Configuration", "steps": [], "code": "// BUGS: missing command, invalid env integer
