}", "language": "json", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "The tools schema allows servers to describe available functions to the host. Each tool definition includes a unique name, description, and input schema formatted according to standard JSON Schema. The LLM reads the description and input schema to decide when and how to format function calls.", "los": ["CO1.LO1"], "sources": ["C1"], "minutes": 6}, {"kind": "concept", "title": "Resources Schema: Exposing File and System Data", "bullets": ["Resources expose readable context identified by uniform resource indicators (URIs).", "Resource definitions include uri, name, description, and optional mimeType.", "Clients retrieve data using resources/read requests with specified URI targets.", "Dynamic resources use URI templates (e.g., file:///{path}) for pattern matching."], "figure": {"kind": "code", "caption": "Resource object definition in an MCP response.", "steps": [], "code": "{
  "resources": [
    {
      "uri": "file:///workspace/pom.xml",
      "name": "Maven Configuration",
      "mimeType": "application/xml"
    }
  ]
}", "language": "json", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "Resources provide context to the LLM without executing actions. A resource is identified by a URI and can carry static file content, database query results, or dynamic logs. The host client uses resources/read to fetch content when the model requires additional context to solve a problem.", "los": ["CO1.LO1"], "sources": ["C1"], "minutes": 6}, {"kind": "concept", "title": "Prompts Schema: Exposing Reusable Workflows", "bullets": ["Prompts expose predefined template instructions with named arguments.", "Servers list available prompts using the prompts/list request handler.", "Clients invoke prompts via prompts/get, passing user arguments into parameters.", "Standardizes context assembly across different AI coding environments."], "figure": {"kind": "code", "caption": "MCP prompt declaration schema.", "steps": [], "code": "{
