}", "language": "json", "rows": []}, "quiz": null, "notes": "Prompts are server-side templates designed to encapsulate complex prompt engineering patterns. Instead of requiring users or IDEs to hardcode prompts, an MCP server can provide tailored prompt templates (e.g., 'generate unit test') with input parameters that client hosts can execute directly.", "los": ["CO1.LO1"], "sources": ["C1"], "minutes": 6}, {"kind": "concept", "title": "Workspace Configuration Files (mcp.json)", "bullets": ["Developer workspaces configure MCP servers via a central configuration schema.", "Defines the mcpServers object containing server identifiers and executable properties.", "Properties include command, args, and env key-value pairs for process execution.", "Enables teams to share consistent agent tool definitions across developer environments."], "figure": {"kind": "code", "caption": "Standard developer workspace configuration file payload.", "steps": [], "code": "{
  "mcpServers": {
